"To solve for \\(i^5 + i^{-25} + i^{45}\\), we need to understand the properties of the imaginary unit \\(i\\). The powers of \\(i\\) cycle every four terms:\n\n\\[\ni^1 = i, \\quad i^2 = -1, \\quad i^3 = -i, \\quad i^4 = 1\n\\]\n\nThis cycle repeats. Therefore, we can simplify each term in the expression:\n\n\\[\ni^5 = i\n\\]\n\\[\ni^{-25} = \\frac{1}{i^{25}} = \\frac{1}{i^5} = \\frac{1}{i} = -i\n\\]\n\\[\ni^{45} = i^{4 \\cdot 11} = (i^4)^{11} = 1\n\\]\n\nNow, we sum these results:\n\n\\[\ni^5 + i^{-25} + i^{45} = i + (-i) + 1 = i - i + 1 = 1\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]"
"To find the annual interest rate, we can use the formula for compound interest:\n\n\\[ A = P(1 + r)^n \\]\n\nwhere:\n- \\( A \\) is the amount of money accumulated after n years, including interest.\n- \\( P \\) is the principal amount (the initial amount of money).\n- \\( r \\) is the annual interest rate (in decimal form).\n- \\( n \\) is the number of years the money is invested for.\n\nGiven:\n- \\( A = 1225 \\)\n- \\( P = 1000 \\)\n- \\( n = 3 \\)\n\nWe need to find \\( r \\):\n\n\\[ 1225 = 1000(1 + r)^3 \\]\n\n\\[ 1.225 = (1 + r)^3 \\]\n\n\\[ 1 + r = \\sqrt[3]{1.225} \\]\n\n\\[ 1 + r \\approx 1.07 \\]\n\n\\[ r \\approx 0.07 \\]\n\nConverting \\( r \\) to a percentage:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{7} \\]"
