"We can use the distributive property to expand the expression:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n(2x^5 + 3x^2)(x^4 - 4x^2 + 3x - 8) &= 2x^5(x^4 - 4x^2 + 3x - 8) + 3x^2(x^4 - 4x^2 + 3x - 8) \\\\\n&= 2x^9 - 8x^7 + 6x^6 - 16x^5 + 3x^6 - 12x^4 + 9x^3 - 24x^2 \\\\\n&= 2x^9 - 8x^7 + 9x^6 - 16x^5 - 12x^4 + 9x^3 - 24x^2.\n\\end{align*}\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $\\boxed{2x^9 - 8x^7 + 9x^6 - 16x^5 - 12x^4 + 9x^3 - 24x^2}$."
