"To find the eighth term of the geometric sequence, we first need to determine the common ratio \\( r \\) and the first term \\( a \\).\n\nThe common ratio \\( r \\) is found by dividing the second term by the first term:\n\\[\nr = \\frac{\\frac{8}{3}}{\\frac{16}{9}} = \\frac{8}{3} \\cdot \\frac{9}{16} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\n\nThe first term \\( a \\) is given as \\( \\frac{16}{9} \\).\n\nThe eighth term \\( a_8 \\) of a geometric sequence is given by:\n\\[\na_8 = a \\cdot r^7\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the values:\n\\[\na_8 = \\frac{16}{9} \\cdot \\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^7 = \\frac{16}{9} \\cdot \\frac{216}{128} = \\frac{3456}{1152}\n\\]\n\nThus, the eighth term of the sequence is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{3456}{1152}}\\)."
