"To simplify \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{72}}{\\sqrt{10}}\\), we can use the property of square roots that states \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{a}}{\\sqrt{b}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{a}{b}}\\). Applying this property, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt{72}}{\\sqrt{10}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{72}{10}}\n\\]\n\nNext, we simplify the fraction inside the square root. The numerator 72 and the denominator 10 have a common factor of 2. We can divide both the numerator and the denominator by 2:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{72}{10} = \\frac{72 \\div 2}{10 \\div 2} = \\frac{36}{5}\n\\]\n\nNow, we take the square root of \\(\\frac{36}{5}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac{36}{5}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{36}}{\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{6}{5}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the simplified form of \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{72}}{\\sqrt{10}}\\) is \\(\\frac{6}{5}\\)."
