"To find the value of \\(\\log_{8}{2938}\\), we need to determine the power to which 8 must be raised to obtain 2938. We can do this by estimating the powers of 8 and finding the appropriate range.\n\nFirst, let's estimate the powers of 8:\n\\[\n8^1 = 8\n\\]\n\\[\n8^2 = 64\n\\]\n\\[\n8^3 = 512\n\\]\n\\[\n8^4 = 4096\n\\]\n\nWe see that:\n\\[\n8^3 = 512 < 2938 < 8^4 = 4096\n\\]\n\nThus, \\(\\log_{8}{2938}\\) is between 3 and 4. Therefore, the consecutive integers \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) between which \\(\\log_{8}{2938}\\) lies are 3 and 4.\n\nTo find \\(a + b\\):\n\\[\na + b = 3 + 4 = 7\n\\]\n\nThus, the answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{7}\n\\]"
