"To determine the number of edges in an octagonal prism, we need to consider the structure of the prism. An octagonal prism has two octagonal bases and eight rectangular faces connecting the corresponding vertices of the bases.\n\n1. Each octagonal base has 8 edges.\n2. Since there are two octagonal bases, the total number of edges from the bases is \\(2 \\times 8 = 16\\).\n3. Each rectangular face has 4 edges.\n4. Since there are eight rectangular faces, the total number of edges from the rectangular faces is \\(8 \\times 4 = 32\\).\n\nAdding these together, the total number of edges in an octagonal prism is:\n\\[ 16 + 32 = 48 \\]\n\nTherefore, an octagonal prism has \\(\\boxed{48}\\) edges."
