"We start by factoring the given polynomial \\(x^8 + 3x^4 - 4\\). Notice that this polynomial can be rewritten as:\n\n\\[\nx^8 + 3x^4 - 4 = (x^4 + 1)^2 - 5\n\\]\n\nThis can be factored using the difference of squares:\n\n\\[\n(x^4 + 1)^2 - 5 = (x^4 + 1 - 2)(x^4 + 1 + 2) = (x^4 - 1)(x^4 + 3)\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to evaluate each factor at \\(x = 1\\):\n\n\\[\np_1(1) = 1^4 - 1 = 0\n\\]\n\\[\np_2(1) = 1^4 + 3 = 4\n\\]\n\nThus, the sum of the evaluations at \\(x = 1\\) is:\n\n\\[\np_1(1) + p_2(1) = 0 + 4 = 4\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is \\( \\boxed{4} \\)."
