"To solve the expression \\(8 - 4 \\div 2 - 1\\), we need to follow the order of operations, often remembered by the acronym PEMDAS (Parentheses, Exponents, Multiplication and Division (from left to right), Addition and Subtraction (from left to right)).\n\n1. First, we perform the division:\n   \\[\n   4 \\div 2 = 2\n   \\]\n   So the expression now becomes:\n   \\[\n   8 - 2 - 1\n   \\]\n\n2. Next, we perform the subtraction:\n   \\[\n   8 - 2 = 6\n   \\]\n   So the expression now becomes:\n   \\[\n   6 - 1\n   \\]\n\n3. Finally, we perform the last subtraction:\n   \\[\n   6 - 1 = 5\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the expression \\(8 - 4 \\div 2 - 1\\) is \\(\\boxed{5}\\)."
