"To determine the number of sides of a polygon where each interior angle measures 170 degrees, we can use the fact that the sum of the interior angles in any polygon is always 180 degrees. Let \\( n \\) be the number of sides of the polygon. The sum of the interior angles of a polygon with \\( n \\) sides is given by the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Sum of interior angles} = 180(n-2)\n\\]\n\nSince each interior angle is 170 degrees, the sum of the interior angles can also be expressed as:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Sum of interior angles} = 170n\n\\]\n\nSetting these two expressions equal to each other, we get:\n\n\\[\n180(n-2) = 170n\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify this equation by dividing both sides by 170:\n\n\\[\n2n-4 = n\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( n \\), we get:\n\n\\[\n2n - n = 4\n\\]\n\n\\[\nn = 4\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the polygon has \\( \\boxed{4} \\) sides."
