"To simplify the expression \\((-k + 4) + (-2 + 3k)\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Distribute the positive sign through the second set of parentheses.\n2. Combine like terms.\n\nLet's start with the first step:\n\n\\[\n(-k + 4) + (-2 + 3k) = -k + 4 - 2 + 3k\n\\]\n\nNext, we combine the like terms. The like terms in this expression are the terms involving \\(k\\) and the constant terms.\n\n\\[\n-k + 4 - 2 + 3k = -k + 3k + (4 - 2)\n\\]\n\nNow, let's combine the \\(k\\) terms:\n\n\\[\n-k + 3k = 2k\n\\]\n\nAnd the constant terms:\n\n\\[\n4 - 2 = 2\n\\]\n\nSo, the expression simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n2k + 2\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the simplified form of \\((-k + 4) + (-2 + 3k)\\) is \\(\\boxed{2k + 2}\\)."
