"To find the percentage of households that eat their dinner together at least once a week, we need to add the percentages of households that eat dinner together for at least one day a week.\n\nFrom the table, we have the following percentages:\n- Households that eat dinner together for 7 days a week: 40%\n- Households that eat dinner together for 5-6 days a week: 30%\n- Households that eat dinner together for 1-4 days a week: 20%\n- Households that eat dinner together for 0 days a week: 10%\n\nNow, we add these percentages together:\n\\[ 40\\% + 30\\% + 20\\% + 10\\% \\]\n\nCalculating the sum:\n\\[ 40\\% + 30\\% = 70\\% \\]\n\\[ 70\\% + 20\\% = 90\\% \\]\n\\[ 90\\% + 10\\% = 100\\% \\]\n\nTherefore, the percentage of households that eat their dinner together at least once a week is \\( \\boxed{100\\%} \\)."
