"First, simplify the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n\\[\n20 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{2}{5}\\right)^2 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)^2 \\cdot \\frac{5}{9}\n\\]\n\nCalculate each term separately:\n\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{2}{5}\\right)^2 = \\frac{4}{25}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)^2 = \\frac{9}{16}\n\\]\n\nNow multiply these results together:\n\n\\[\n20 \\cdot \\frac{4}{25} \\cdot \\frac{9}{16} \\cdot \\frac{5}{9} = 20 \\cdot \\frac{1}{40} = \\frac{20}{40} = \\frac{1}{2}\n\\]\n\nNext, raise the result to the power of 5:\n\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^5 = \\frac{1}{32}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{32}}\n\\]"
